CITY CONTRACT#
Date: L/8/21
MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING
BETWEEN JOHNSON COUNTY, WYOMING, AND
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING,
FOR EXTRATERRITORIAL LAW ENFORCEMENT ASSISTANCE
This Memorandum of Understanding("MOU") is by and between Johnson County,
Wyoming(Johnson County"), whose address is 76North Main Street, Buffalo, Wyoming 82834,
and the City of Cheyenne, a Wyoming municipal corporation(Cityof Cheyenne'), whose address
is Municipal Building,2101 O'Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.Johnson County and
effective upon the date of thelast signature affixed hereto.
RECITALS:
WHEREAS, pursuant toW.S.7-2-106(b), Johnson County and the City of Cheyenne are
authorized toenterinto an MOU for the purpose of providing extraterritorial law enforcement
assistance to the other Party's law enforcement agency; and
immediate manpower, skill, and equipment capacities of either Party's law enforcement agency,
Johnson County and the City of Cheyenne mayrequest that the other Party provide certified peace
officers for law enforcement assistance.
NOW, THEREFORE, subject to the limitations of this MOU and the provisions of W.S.
7-2-106, the Parties agree as follows:
1. Purpose. The purpose of this MOU is to permit each Party to assign certified peace
officers to the other Party for law enforcement assistance within the jurisdictional boundaries of
Johnson County and the City of Cheyenne, as requested by the law enforcement agencies of the
Parties.Neither Party has a duty to provide law enforcement assistance under this MOU.Each
assistance from the other Party and each Partyhas discretionary authority to determine the nature
and extent ofits response. In the event a Party agrees to respond to a request from the other Party,
the following terms and conditions shall apply.
2.Term.This MOU shall not be effective until it is approved by all of the Parties.
ThisMOU shall beinfull force and effect from thedatethat thisMOUis executed by the Parties
and shall remain in effect fora period of time not to exceed one(1) month beyond the current term
of office of any participating Chief of Police or Sheriff.Either Party may terminate this MOU by
giving the other Party thirty(30)days written notice of its intent to terminate.
MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING
BETWEEN JOHNSON COUNTY, WYOMING, AND
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING
FOR EXTRATERRITORIAL LAW ENFORCEMENT ASSISTANCE
